A history entry where only condition-set descriptions changed never collapses to a count, unlike every other type of condition-set change. Edit the description field on more than three condition sets in a single flag save and you can see it.

`summarize` is computed once from `added.length + changed.length + diff.removed.length > MAX_DETAILED_SET_CHANGES`, so it is true as soon as more than 3 sets are touched. The rollout, criteria, variant, and added branches all route their sentence through `listOrCount`, which reads `summarize` and swaps the list of names for a count. The `descriptionOnly` branch instead calls `joinInline` directly over every touched set, without checking `summarize`.

So the sentence names every set individually ("changed the description of condition set 1, condition set 2, condition set 3, condition set 4 and condition set 5") instead of collapsing to "changed the description of 5 condition sets", which contradicts the behavior the PR itself states for touching more than three sets.

Route the description-only branch through `listOrCount` the same way the other branches do, and add a test that edits the description of 4+ condition sets in one save and asserts the sentence reads as a count rather than naming every set.

```diff
     if (descriptionOnly.length) {
-        parts.push(
-            <>
-                changed the description of{' '}
-                {joinInline(descriptionOnly.map((set) => <>condition set {set.index + 1}</>))}
-            </>
-        )
+        const verbs = { detail: 'changed the description of', count: 'changed the description of' }
+        parts.push(listOrCount(descriptionOnly, verbs, (set) => <>condition set {set.index + 1}</>))
     }
```

The new Release conditions tab is attached to a history entry, and becomes the default tab, even when the condition-set diff found no actual change to show. That happens on any filters edit where `filtersAfter.groups` is present but no condition set actually changed: a multivariate payload-only edit, or any other filters-field edit where the sets are byte-identical.

`activityDescriptions.tsx:237` attaches `expandedView` whenever `filtersAfter.groups` is an array, without checking whether the condition-set diff produced any added, changed, or removed sets. [`ActivityLog.tsx:149`](https://github.com/PostHog/posthog/blob/66b1c1750c57b7040cbb0a179d96f60e02e16853/frontend/src/lib/components/ActivityLog/ActivityLog.tsx#L149) then defaults the row to the tab that renders `expandedView.label`, which is the Release conditions tab.

So the history row opens on Release conditions showing three untagged, unchanged cards, while the Diff tab that actually shows what changed is one click away.

Only attach `expandedView` when the condition-set diff actually produced a change, e.g. compute `describeConditionSetChanges` first and gate the `expandedView` assignment on its length being non-zero. A test for a multivariate payload-only edit (or another filters edit that doesn't touch condition sets), asserting no `expandedView` is attached, would cover it.

